Update guidance:
Preserve the documented ~/.jcode/worker-blueprints/ default, including
symlinked directories and Markdown files. The reserved coordinator ID
must never be accepted as an ordinary worker blueprint or generate a
swarm_coordinator tool. The coordinator.md front matter accepts only
enabled-tools and disabled-tools; no name, description, model, effort,
communication-policy, or timeout-minutes. The [agents.worker_blueprints.
coordinator] override accepts only enabled and disabled; worker-only
fields (model, effort, timeout_minutes) are rejected. Preserve the
precedence chain for model (per-spawn > blueprint > swarm_model >
coordinator) and timeout (per-call > blueprint > config > default 20m).
Generated swarm_<id> descriptions are user-owned and exempt from the
static built-in description token cap. Worker completion prompts must
request a final assistant response and must not require unavailable swarm
tools. Blueprint enabled-tools are
always combined with the global tool policy. Coordinator policy only
applies to root sessions, never to spawned workers or internal roles.
The coordinator.md body is injected as a stable static segment in the
root system prompt only when swarm is enabled. Communication-policy none
blocks ordinary messages but not tool results. Generated tools default
to headless execution. Generated tools never overwrite existing tool
names. All test SwarmMember and WorkerBlueprintOverride constructions
must include the new fields. Spawn summaries and report-scope follow-ups
must use the same final_report text so summary offsets stay valid.
Transcript scope must stay newest-first and label its direction. Protocol
validation must include provider-core tests to exercise upstream Tokio macro
feature unification.

